WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.965
Provenance Is the New Professionalism. A polished answer is not

2
00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:09.929
automatically a reliable answer. In a world full of drafts

3
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:14.894
that sound complete, provenance is what lets another person check

4
00:00:14.894 --> 00:00:19.858
the work. Professionalism now includes a simple record: what source

5
00:00:19.858 --> 00:00:24.823
was used, what claim was made, what limitation applies, who

6
00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:29.788
reviewed it, and what decision followed. Use a four-line record.

7
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:34.752
For a consequential output, record the source set, the material

8
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:39.717
claim, the reviewer, and the action taken. This takes minutes

9
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:44.682
and saves hours when a question returns later. Keep drafts

10
00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:49.646
in their place. AI can help organize, compare, and draft.

11
00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:54.611
It should not erase the difference between a source-backed conclusion

12
00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:59.575
and a plausible-sounding suggestion. Make correction ordinary. A provenance record

13
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:04.540
makes revision less personal. When new evidence appears, update the

14
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.505
claim and explain the change. That is how a system

15
00:01:09.505 --> 00:01:14.469
earns trust over time. Beacon’s source-grounded brief checker is a

16
00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:17.448
simple starting point for the practice.
